labels={'E0':'Technical only E0','E1':'Archived direct news E1','E1B':'Compact direct news E1B',**{f'E2_h{h}':f'Equation E2 with {h} hour half life' for h in [3,6,12,24]}}
protocol='All candidates retain 19 technical inputs, including real BTC close, and 30 hourly observations ending at the forecast origin. The target is the XRP log return exactly 24 hours later. The chronological training block has 18,861 origins; validation has the same 2,136 origins as E0 and E1, from 19 December 2025 at 07:00 UTC through 18 March 2026 at 06:00 UTC. Training labels finish before validation begins. Evaluation labels remain redacted and no final evaluation inference was performed.'
training='The model is a two-layer BiLSTM with 128 hidden units per direction, dropout 0.2, a 256-to-64 ReLU dense layer, dropout 0.2 and one scalar output. There is no attention. Adam uses learning rate 0.001 and batch size 32, up to 200 epochs with patience 15. Each seed retains the minimum validation scaled-return MSE checkpoint. Configurations are ranked by mean reconstructed-price validation RMSE across seeds 42, 123, 2026, 7 and 99. Robust input scaling is fitted only on unique training-window rows; MinMax target scaling is fitted only on training returns and matches E0.'
limits='Publication time rounded up to the next hour is a retrospective availability proxy, not verified first-public availability. All 19,928 article records lack verified first-public flags; missing coverage is not proof that no relevant news occurred. Scores are model-derived judgments, not measured causal price impacts. No news was timed using future price movements. E1B and E2 share the current archive, whereas E1 uses its preserved earlier news construction; improvement over E1 can reflect coverage and preprocessing as well as feature design. Five seeds measure optimisation variability within one market period, not five independent market replications. Validation was used for selection; intervals do not correct all selection optimism. Previously examined 2026 data is not a pristine prospective test.'
statmethod='Paired circular moving-block bootstrap uses 2,000 resamples, fixed seed 2026, primary 72-hour blocks and 24/168-hour sensitivities. It compares the square root of mean squared error averaged over seeds and times; this risk estimand differs slightly from the arithmetic mean of five seed RMSEs used for ranking. Negative differences favour the new candidate. The 98.75% intervals apply Bonferroni adjustment to four E3 comparisons against E0, E1, E1B and E2 with 6 hour half life; 95% intervals are also saved. Overlapping 24-hour targets motivate block resampling. The preselected validation winner still needs independent replication.'
def newdoc(title):
 d=Document();s=d.sections[0];s.top_margin=s.bottom_margin=Inches(.65);s.left_margin=s.right_margin=Inches(.75)
 for name in ['Normal','Title','Heading 1','Heading 2','Caption']:
  st=d.styles[name];st.font.name='Calibri';st.font.color.rgb=RGBColor(0,0,0)
 d.styles['Normal'].font.size=Pt(10);d.styles['Normal'].paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(6);d.styles['Title'].font.size=Pt(21);d.styles['Heading 1'].font.size=Pt(13)
 for e in list(d.styles.element.iter(qn('w:pBdr'))):e.getparent().remove(e)
 d.add_paragraph(title,'Title');return d
def table(d,head,rows):
 t=d.add_table(rows=1,cols=len(head));t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
 for c,x in zip(t.rows[0].cells,head):c.text=str(x)
 for row in rows:
  for c,x in zip(t.add_row().cells,row):c.text=str(x)
 d.add_paragraph('')
def pic(d,p,caption):d.add_picture(str(p),width=Inches(6.6));d.add_paragraph(caption,'Caption')
def equation(d,text):
 p=d.add_paragraph();m=OxmlElement('m:oMath');r=OxmlElement('m:r');t=OxmlElement('m:t');t.text=text;r.append(t);m.append(r);p._p.append(m)
def pageheading(d,title):
 p=d.add_heading(title,1);p.paragraph_format.page_break_before=True
def save_doc(d,path):
 for table_ in d.tables:
  for ri,row_ in enumerate(table_.rows):
   for cell in row_.cells:
    pr=cell._tc.get_or_add_tcPr();b=OxmlElement('w:tcBorders')
    for side in ['top','left','bottom','right']:
     edge=OxmlElement('w:'+side);edge.set(qn('w:val'),'single');edge.set(qn('w:sz'),'4');edge.set(qn('w:color'),'D9D9D9');b.append(edge)
    pr.append(b)
    if ri==0:
     sh=OxmlElement('w:shd');sh.set(qn('w:fill'),'D9E5F2');pr.append(sh)
 d.save(path)
 # Companion Markdown retains the narrative and all table values.
 lines=[]
 for p in d.paragraphs:
  mathtext=''.join(e.text or '' for e in p._p.iter(qn('m:t')))
  if mathtext:lines.append(mathtext)
  if p.text:lines.append(('# ' if p.style.name=='Title' else '## ' if p.style.name.startswith('Heading') else '')+p.text)
 for t in d.tables:
  lines.append('\n'+'\n'.join(' | '.join(c.text for c in row.cells) for row in t.rows))
 path.with_suffix('.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines))
